# Charts & analytics — Bklit reference

For any analytics, KPIs, or chart UI in the web app, **refer to [bklit.com](https://bklit.com)** (gallery + docs) as the visual and interaction reference. Prefer patterns from:

- https://bklit.com/charts/bar-chart
- https://bklit.com/docs/components/bar-chart
- https://bklit.com/docs/theming

## Visual language (match even when staying on Recharts / shadcn Chart)

- **Card shell:** title + muted subtitle above the plot; optional footer insight (trend line) below.
- **Grid:** horizontal dashed lines only; no heavy vertical grid.
- **Bars:** solid series fill, flat or lightly rounded tops, generous band gap; primary series uses faded brand blue `#1A16F3` (e.g. `color-mix(in srgb, #1A16F3 50%, white)` or equivalent soft opacity) — not neon-saturated.
- **Axes:** tick labels muted; no axis line / tick marks unless needed.
- **Chrome:** quiet borders (`ring-1` / hairline), ample padding, no decorative badges on the chart itself.
- **Series tokens:** keep `--chart-1`…`--chart-5` aligned with brand; avoid default purple chart stacks.

## When adding new charts

1. Open the matching Bklit gallery example first and mirror layout density, grid, and footer treatment.
2. Reuse `@/components/ui/chart` (`ChartContainer` + config) unless product explicitly adopts Bklit components.
3. Do not invent a second analytics aesthetic (glow bars, heavy gradients, pill legends in the plot area).
